<Base title="About — Islamic Tech Guide"><article class="prose panel doc-page"><div class="eyebrow">Project vision</div><h1>About the guide</h1><p>Islamic Tech Guide is an open-source map of technology resources related to Muslim communities: applications, websites, services, developer tools, libraries, APIs, platforms and other useful digital surfaces.</p><p>Its purpose is to make the ecosystem legible: archive what exists, assess it progressively, expose imbalances, and help developers and contributors decide where effort may be more valuable.</p><p>Developers, contributors and builders are the primary audience. End users — especially Arabic-speaking users — are secondary users who may benefit from faster discovery.</p><p>It is intentionally not a general Islamic books/PDF library. Datasets are not a collection priority at this stage.</p><p class="arabic-copy" dir="rtl">الهدف هو أرشفة المشهد التقني المرتبط باحتياجات المجتمع المسلم، وتقييم الموجود، وإظهار الفجوات وعدم توازن الجهد بصورة تساعد على اتخاذ قرارات أفضل.</p></article></Base>
